@startuml
title Customer App → API → SQL/Redis → SignalR → Admin/POS
autonumber
actor Customer
participant "Mobile App" as App
participant "ASP.NET Core API" as API
database "SQL Server" as SQL
collections "Redis (inventory holds, TTL 15m)" as Redis
participant "NotificationHub" as Hub
participant "Web Admin" as Admin
participant "POS screen" as POS

== UpdateProfile ==
Customer -> App: Edit profile and tap Save
App -> API: PUT /api/storefront/account
activate API
API -> SQL: Validate and update Customer (+ linked User)
SQL --> API: Commit
API -> API: UpdateProfile() / Sync customer cache
API -> Hub: BroadcastToWeb("CustomerUpdated", customer)
Hub -> Admin: CustomerUpdated(customer)
Admin -> Admin: Update row and customer statistics
API --> App: Updated profile
deactivate API

== ReserveStock (when Redis hold endpoint is enabled) ==
Customer -> App: Add product to cart
App -> API: POST /api/storefront/cart/reservations
activate API
API -> SQL: Read Inventory.Quantity
API -> Redis: ReserveStock(customer, product, quantity, TTL=15m)
Redis --> API: Reserved / available quantity
API -> Hub: BroadcastStock("StockReserved", product, available)
Hub -> Admin: StockReserved(product, available)
Hub -> POS: StockReserved(product, available)
API --> App: Reservation result
deactivate API

== CheckoutOrder ==
Customer -> App: Confirm checkout
App -> API: POST /api/storefront/orders
activate API
API -> SQL: Begin transaction; validate and decrement Inventory; insert Order
SQL --> API: Commit
API -> Redis: Release customer's holds
API -> Hub: BroadcastToWeb("NewOrderPlaced", order)
API -> Hub: BroadcastStock("StockUpdated", productIds)
Hub -> Admin: NewOrderPlaced(order)
Hub -> POS: NewOrderPlaced(order)
Hub -> Admin: StockUpdated(productIds)
Hub -> POS: StockUpdated(productIds)
Admin -> Admin: Refresh orders, invoices, stock
POS -> POS: Notify staff and refresh orders/stock
API --> App: Order confirmation
deactivate API

note over API,Redis
The current repository has no Redis client, reservation endpoint,
or Redis connection setting yet. The reservation section is the
required next integration; SQL inventory remains authoritative.
end note
@enduml
